        <div class="about-layout">
            <div class="about-narrative">
                <h2>Professional Journey</h2>
                <p>
                    I started at Washington State DOT in construction inspection and progressed through the ranks
                    to my current role as Bridge Engineer 4 / Database & Application Specialist. My 20 years of tenure
                    have given me deep institutional knowledge of bridge data systems — from the physical structure
                    up through the data that manages it.
                </p>
                <p>
                    As a daily user of AASHTOWare BrM for bridge inventory management and inspection workflows,
                    I see firsthand how bridge management software impacts engineering decisions across our
                    8,400+ structure inventory. That hands-on experience — combined with my development skills —
                    gives me a unique perspective on what bridge engineers actually need from their tools.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Currently, I'm leading the migration of multiple legacy Microsoft Access applications —
                    including the Bridge Condition Report and Seismic Retrofit Status Module — to a modern
                    Blazor Server web front-end backed by SQL Server. This consolidates fragmented bridge
                    data systems into a unified Structure Asset Management (SAM) platform serving 50+
                    engineers and inspectors statewide, replacing workflows that previously required manual
                    data entry across disconnected databases.
                </p>
                <p>
                    My experience spans the full lifecycle: field inspection, data collection, database design,
                    application development, reporting, and decision support. I've recovered 8+ years of unlogged
                    batch records via Python/pdfplumber extraction, remediated broken database views, and built
                    comprehensive documentation where none existed. I regularly train team members on new systems
                    and work directly with bridge inspectors and project engineers to translate their needs into
                    working software.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Outside of WSDOT, I founded NW OpsBridge Automations — a consulting business bringing
                    automation and AI tools to trades and service businesses. Strong mechanical aptitude
                    (transmission rebuilds, welding, electronics) combined with software engineering means
                    I understand both the physical infrastructure and the data systems that manage it.
                </p>

